phism <MATH_0006> induces an isomorphism <MATH_0007>.\nWe are going to define the stack of elliptic curves <MATH_0008>.\nIn the rest of the Stacks project we work out the method introduced in\nDeligne and Mumford's paper <REF_0001> which consists in presenting\n<MATH_0009> as a category endowed with a functor\n<MATH_0010>\nThis means you work with fibred categories over the categories of schemes,\ntopologies, stacks fibred in groupoids, coverings, etc, etc.\nIn this chapter we throw all of that out of the window and\nwe think about it a bit differently -- probably closer to how the initiators\nof the theory started thinking about it themselves.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a74522712d7a57c8dc1880143e77c118450ace90853c9d532c474fc10778cda8", "unit_id": "inventory:stacks-introduction:072J:paragraph/0002"}}}, {"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:stacks-introduction:072K:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:560ad8e3560306aefd500ee1e34426c14110f355e44d3bb19afc5a2a18dada24", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 2679, "byte_start": 2636, "file": "stacks-introduction.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:e53eafa3c0db88d88d335cf81539e5eea2f2fcca9d469c9ab258b7199e25e7e0", "line_end": 85, "line_start": 84}, "owner_tag": "072K", "parent_tag": "072K", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "stacks-introduction", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "072K", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:586210d0cf9ed4621462f9e5ec0ebaf0c3465f0d9473832ae86369ac1f3b2476", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is what we are going to do:\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:477c39ad0f27e4a2dedc5606ef4438d2d08cada6dd633151ea20411